---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import nessie from "../assets/nessie.jpg";
---

<Layout title="Sniffr — Software for dog-care businesses, built around the dog">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 md:gap-16 items-center">
      <div class="md:col-span-7 order-2 md:order-1">
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          Most dog software is built around the bill.<br />
          <span class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">Sniffr is built around the dog.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-8 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] measure">
          Scheduling, intake, photos, payments, and walk reports for dog-care businesses.
          Built alongside a real one, Hamilton Bark, who run about 130 walks a week on
          Sniffr today.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <a
            href="#book"
            class="bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-bg)] px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-medium hover:bg-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors"
          >
            Book a setup call
          </a>
          <a
            href="/roadmap"
            class="text-[var(--color-ink)] underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-accent)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] px-2 py-3"
          >
            See the roadmap &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Here because your walker uses Sniffr?
          <a
            href="https://app.sniffrpack.com"
            class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-accent)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)]"
          >
            Open the app &rarr;
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="md:col-span-5 order-1 md:order-2">
        <figure class="bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_60px_-20px_rgba(184,80,30,0.25)] max-w-sm mx-auto md:ml-auto md:mr-0 ring-1 ring-[var(--color-rule)]">
          <Image
            src={nessie}
            alt="Nessie, a golden retriever, resting close to the camera"
            widths={[400, 600, 800]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 80vw, 400px"
            class="w-full aspect-[3/4] object-cover"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
          <figcaption class="p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <span class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Nessie</span>
              <span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider">Today</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
              "Saw the bagel. Queue Operation Drool."
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">💧 drool deployed</span>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">🥯 bagel watch</span>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">💛 regular</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="currentColor" class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">
                <circle cx="20" cy="22" r="6"/>
                <circle cx="44" cy="22" r="6"/>
                <circle cx="12" cy="36" r="5"/>
                <circle cx="52" cy="36" r="5"/>
                <ellipse cx="32" cy="44" rx="14" ry="11"/>
              </svg>
              <span>A Sniffr memory</span>
            </div>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Showcase: a day in your dog's life -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
          A day in your dog's life, kept.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] measure">
          Every walk leaves something behind. Sniffr turns the day into a record that
          belongs to the dog.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 md:gap-10 items-start">
        <!-- Walk-report timeline card (larger, leads) -->
        <figure class="md:col-span-7 bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_60px_-20px_rgba(184,80,30,0.2)] ring-1 ring-[var(--color-rule)] p-6 md:p-7">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <span class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Biscuit</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider">Today</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed italic">
            "On the way to the dog park he saw an ambulance on 6th and sang the song of
            his people."
          </p>

          <ol class="mt-6 space-y-5">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <div class="flex flex-col items-center pt-1">
                <span class="text-base leading-none">🐕</span>
                <span class="w-px flex-1 min-h-[1.25rem] bg-[var(--color-rule)] mt-2"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="pb-1">
                <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider">Pickup</p>
                <p class="text-base">leash-ready</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <div class="flex flex-col items-center pt-1">
                <span class="text-base leading-none">🚑🎶</span>
                <span class="w-px flex-1 min-h-[1.25rem] bg-[var(--color-rule)] mt-2"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="pb-1">
                <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider">6th &amp; Main</p>
                <p class="text-base">ambulance song</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <div class="flex flex-col items-center pt-1">
                <span class="text-base leading-none">🐾</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider">Dog park</p>
                <p class="text-base">played with Goldie</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="currentColor" class="text-[var(--color-accent)]">
              <circle cx="20" cy="22" r="6"/>
              <circle cx="44" cy="22" r="6"/>
              <circle cx="12" cy="36" r="5"/>
              <circle cx="52" cy="36" r="5"/>
              <ellipse cx="32" cy="44" rx="14" ry="11"/>
            </svg>
            <span>A Sniffr walk report</span>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <!-- Memory / photo moment card (smaller, offset) -->
        <figure class="md:col-span-5 md:mt-14 bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_60px_-20px_rgba(184,80,30,0.2)] ring-1 ring-[var(--color-rule)]">
          <div class="aspect-[4/3] bg-[var(--color-bg)] flex items-center justify-center border-b border-[var(--color-rule)]">
            <svg width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="currentColor" class="text-[var(--color-rule)]">
              <circle cx="20" cy="22" r="6"/>
              <circle cx="44" cy="22" r="6"/>
              <circle cx="12" cy="36" r="5"/>
              <circle cx="52" cy="36" r="5"/>
              <ellipse cx="32" cy="44" rx="14" ry="11"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="p-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
              <span class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Goldie</span>
              <span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] uppercase tracking-wider">Sunday</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
              "Caught mid-zoomie at the park, per usual."
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">🌀 zoomies</span>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-rule)]">🐕‍🦺 with Biscuit</span>
            </div>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Humans and dogs have been shaping each other since before written language
          existed. They notice what we can't, faster and farther than we can, and in
          return one person keeps them safe for the whole of their life. That bargain is
          older than the alphabet, and it still runs every morning at your dog park. We
          think software for dog care should be built the way the bargain is: around the
          dog.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            href="/why"
            class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium hover:underline"
          >
            Read why we built it this way &rarr;
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 3: QR / Intake -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Onboarding
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Your business card is your intake form.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Hand a prospect a card. They scan the QR. Five minutes later, they've signed up,
          told you everything you need to know about their dog, picked a payment method,
          and landed on your Google Calendar for a Meet &amp; Greet.
        </p>
        <p>
          You did no data entry. They did no email tag. Every Sniffr card is a tracked
          invite — you'll know which card brought which client, and which conversations
          turned into customers.
        </p>
        <p>
          By the time you say hello at the M&amp;G, you already know their dog's name,
          their vet, and how often they want to walk.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 4: Windows / Horizon -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Scheduling Model
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Sell Windows. Walks happen automatically.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Recurring dog care isn't a calendar full of appointments you re-book every week.
          It's a handful of standing commitments. Sniffr's scheduling is shaped like that.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <strong>Window</strong> is a standing arrangement: <em>"Wednesday evenings
          between 6 and 7:30, 30 minutes with Wally."</em> You sell those once. Walks get
          generated every week the Window is active.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <strong>Horizon</strong> is how far ahead you lock walks in. Some walkers run
          three days out, some run three weeks. Solo walker or twenty-walker shop, you set
          how far you plan. Raise it as your team grows.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pricing is captured the moment a Window is created. Payment doesn't run until
          the Horizon is locked. Predictable cash flow on a cadence you control — not
          a per-walk billing scramble.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 5: Voice / Reports -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Walk Reports
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Talk through the walk. Sniffr listens.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Walkers don't have to be writers. Tell Sniffr what happened on the walk — out
          loud — and we'll turn it into a tagged, searchable timeline for the dog.
        </p>

        <p>
          Each moment becomes a structured event on the dog's timeline, tagged with emojis,
          searchable across weeks. Snap photos along the way. Caption them yourself; we'll
          handle the hashtags. Write a full walk report when it matters; skip it when the
          audio and photos already tell the story.
        </p>

        <p>
          For a walker doing 20+ walks a week, this is the single biggest time-saver in
          Sniffr. Roughly 10 minutes of paperwork per walk &mdash; gone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 6: Scheduling intelligence -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Scheduling Intelligence
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Sniffr learns who walks who.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Most software needs you to tell it who walks Goldie. Sniffr figures it out.
        </p>
        <p>
          After a few weeks, Sniffr knows that Sarah is Goldie's regular &mdash; not because
          you set a rule, but because Sarah has actually been walking Goldie for eight
          weeks. New Wednesday Windows route to Sarah automatically.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sniffr also predicts the time <em>within</em> the Window. Sarah's been arriving
          around 6:15 each week, not 6:00 sharp. The next walk gets scheduled for 6:15,
          with a confidence score. Reassignments suggest the right replacement and won't
          let you double-book.
        </p>
        <p class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl pt-4 text-[var(--color-accent)]">
          The longer you run on Sniffr, the better it gets at running itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 7: Your business -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Ownership
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Your business. Your Stripe. Your customers.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Sniffr is software, not a marketplace.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bring your own Stripe Connect account. Hire your own employees. Set your own
          rates. Charge whatever you charge &mdash; Sniffr never touches your customer
          relationships. When you leave us, your customers come with you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We don't take a cut of your customer revenue. We don't broker your relationships.
          We don't decide who can work for you.
        </p>
        <p class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl pt-4">
          This is the whole stance. It's the reason Sniffr exists.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 8: Roadmap teaser -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32 bg-white/40">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        What's next
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        Sniffr ships fast.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Self-serve walker signup, AI-assisted reports, walker-to-walker work sharing,
          the dog's own record opening to every family, the social layer that turns dog
          parks into Packs and dogs into Circles, and service plugins beyond walks &mdash;
          shipping in that order, through 2026 and into 2027.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/roadmap"
          class="inline-block mt-4 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium hover:underline"
        >
          See the full roadmap &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 9: Hamilton Bark proof -->
  <section class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-accent)] font-semibold">
        Built with
      </p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mt-3 text-balance">
        A real dog-walking business.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-3 gap-6 md:gap-10 max-w-2xl">
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-accent)]">130</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-1">walks per week</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-accent)]">6</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-1">walkers on staff</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-accent)]">$250K</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-1">annual service revenue</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          <strong>Hamilton Bark</strong> runs everything you've read about above on Sniffr,
          today. Every feature listed survives contact with that business or it doesn't ship.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sniffr launched after a year of building against a real production customer.
          Not in a sandbox. Not in a pitch deck. In a working dog-walking business with
          paying clients and a payroll.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="mx-auto max-w-5xl border-[var(--color-rule)]" />

  <!-- Screen 10: CTA -->
  <section id="book" class="px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
        Ready to switch?
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-8 text-lg md:text-xl text-[var(--color-muted)] measure mx-auto">
        If you're running 1&ndash;10 walkers and you've felt the limits of Time To Pet,
        Scout, or Precise &mdash; or you're starting a business and you want to start it
        right &mdash; let's talk. Setup calls are 30 minutes, run by the founder, and
        cover data migration, Stripe Connect, and walker training.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
        Sniffr is free until your fourth client pays.
        <a
          href="/pricing"
          class="underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-accent)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)]"
        >
          See pricing &rarr;
        </a>
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="mailto:joseph@papyruslabs.ai?subject=Sniffr%20setup%20call"
          class="bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-bg)] px-8 py-4 rounded-md font-medium text-lg hover:bg-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors"
        >
          Book a setup call
        </a>
        <a
          href="/roadmap"
          class="text-[var(--color-ink)] underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[var(--color-accent)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] px-2 py-4"
        >
          See the roadmap first &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
